name krxn1 krxn2  (calibrated 2026-10-25 against IPCC 2019 rice CH4 (1.19 kg/ha/d): reference soil, 15-cell grid, reactions incl. g2o2, nh4up, rtoxy (root O2 loss 10 mmol/m2/d), --phd=14 --ch4ph=6.2:7.9:6.5 --nucl=cc:0.001 --kscale=maf:0.45,fsp:0.25; flooded 1.17 kg/ha/d). v5 (2026-10-25): N2O-reductase pH50 5.5 (was 6), keeping acid-soil (pH ~5) N2O at 2.3 kg N/ha/season vs 1.8 at pH 6.5; pH50 6 gave 15-28 kg N/ha at pH 5) v6 (2026-10-26): calibrated on the settled season+fallow cycle (paddy/multiyear/run_chain.sh, 3 yr after the fallow spin-up, OMF 0.7) with no methanogen pH response (no --ch4ph), --n2c=0.03 (straw/root inputs) and the Si feedback on root O2 loss --rtsi=5e-4:2.7e-4:0.5; g2ch4 vmax 950 (900 gave 128 kg CH4/ha/season at year 4) v7 (2026-10-26): as v6 plus O2 inhibition constant of all anaerobic pathways 2.5e-7 M (--o2inh=2.5e-7; was 2.52e-5, which left ~9% of anaerobic rates in aerated soil and gave ~7 kg N2O-N/ha in the fallow); g2ch4 vmax 1600 (1750 gave 151 kg CH4/ha/season) v8 (2026-10-26): same constants as v7 plus rice Si uptake (reaction siup, default 3.7 mol Si/m2/yr, Km 0.3 mM) and soil amorphous-silica rate x30 (--kscale=maf:0.45,fsp:0.25,amsi:30), giving porewater Si 0.19 mM and uptake 130 kg Si/ha/season without basalt; Si feedback w 0.5 (--rtsi=5e-4:2.7e-4:0.5, fits Gong -18% at w~0.53). Flooded 129 kg CH4/ha/season, AWD/flooded 0.71. Full production options: --o2inh=2.5e-7 --n2c=0.03 --rtsi=5e-4:2.7e-4:0.5 --kscale=maf:0.45,fsp:0.25,amsi:30 --nucl=cc:0.001, no --ch4ph, settled cycle via paddy/multiyear/run_chain.sh (3 yr, OMF 0.7), exe from makefile_paddy_fast v9 (2026-10-26): multi-year baseline without drift: percolation --q=0.1 (well-puddled paddy with a plough pan; at 0.5 m/yr Fe2+ leaching drains the plough layer's reducible Fe and control CH4 rises ~6%/yr, as in leaky 'akiochi' soils), puddling depth 0.2 m (run_chain.sh TILL=0.2), siderite oxidation (sidox), Fe(III) input --fe3in=0.3; g2ch4 vmax 2100 (1600/2400/3200 gave ~87/155/215 kg CH4/ha/season on the settled cycle). Production options: as v8 plus --q=0.1 --fe3in=0.3, TILL=0.2, exe scepter_paddy_v10 v9.1 (2026-10-26): g2n2p vmax 1000 (was 300): season N2O 0.40 kg N2O-N/ha with 120 kg urea-N and a pre-harvest drain (300 gave 1.7; Akiyama et al. 2005 flooded-rice EF 0.31% -> ~0.4 kg); CH4 unchanged pH-response sensitivity case (--ch4ph=6.2:7.9:6.5, Si w 0): use paddy/krxn_calibrated_v9_ph.in (g2ch4 vmax 3600; 3500 gave ~125 kg CH4/season on the settled cycle, 2100 gave 68) v11 (2026-10-26): after fixing the squared Fe2+ concentration in fe2o2 (exe scepter_paddy_v11), drift is ~0.8%/yr at realistic percolation, so the reference is back to --q=0.5 (1.4 mm/d; 0.1 gave a nitrate-rich, acid, CH4-free soil); g2ch4 vmax 1500 (1400/1700 gave 117/149 kg CH4/ha/season at year 2). Production options: as v9 with --q=0.5, exe scepter_paddy_v11, TILL=0.2 v12 (2026-10-27): CH4 ebullition rate constant 1000/yr (was 100; deep pCH4 reached 0.8 atm and vented after harvest as a fallow pulse equal to the season emission at rainfed sites); rainfed sites also get the 14-day pre-harvest drain (--awd --phd=14). g2ch4 vmax 1350 (1200/1400 gave 108/134 kg CH4/ha/season at year 3); fallow CH4 now ~15 kg (~11% of the season); AWD/flooded 0.66. v13 (2026-10-27): pH-dependent N2O yield of denitrification (--n2oy=6.2:1:0.1, exe scepter_paddy_v13): a fraction 0.1 + 0.9/(1+10^(pH-6.2)) of NO3- denitrified stops at N2O, the rest goes to N2 in the same microsites (N2O/(N2O+N2) falls with pH; Simek and Cooper 2002, Liu et al. 2010, Russenes et al. 2016). Without it, the upstream pH-7 optimum of denitrification made basalt triple fallow N2O in acid soils. g2n2p vmax 300 (150/400/1000 gave 0.83/0.27/0.11 kg N2O-N/ha/season on the reference control, target ~0.4). v15 (2026-10-27): explicit pH-dependent rhizosphere oxidation of plant-transported CH4 (--pox=0.3:0.9:6:1, reaction ch4rx, exe scepter_paddy_v15) in place of the fixed Pox 0.5, and plant CH4 conductance ch4pl 1100 (was 300; ebullition had carried 42-67% of emission vs ~10-20% in the field). n2opl 0.207 keeps the absolute plant N2O conductance of v13. g2ch4 vmax 1630 (1350/1800 gave 110/148 kg CH4/ha/season at year 3); reference control 132-135 kg CH4, 0.36 kg N2O-N/season. Prompted by lime (5 studies) and steel-slag (Wang et al. 2014) trials: slag 2/4/8 t/ha now -24/-27/-30% (v13 -20/-19/-16%, observed -27/-43/-49%). v16 (2026-10-27): green-rust bioavailability to Fe(III) reducers 1.0 (was 0.3; g2gr krxn2), removing a tuned constant. Reference control unchanged (135.0 kg CH4, 0.36 kg N2O-N/season); Gong 36 t/ha -21% (v15 -19%, obs -18%); Park -20/-34% (v15 -15/-28%, obs -25/-37%); slag -24/-27/-31%; lime (irr043, 3.3 t/ha) yr1 -12%, yr2 +2% (v15 -8/+5.5%, obs -20 to -53%): lime remains a misfit. Same options and exe as v15.
g2ch4 1860 30
g2fe3 300 -999
g2so4 300 -999
ch4pl 1100 -999
g2n21 300 -999
g2n2p 300 5.5
g2gr -999 1.0
rtco2 60 -999
amo2o 30 -999
ch4eb 1000 -999
n2opl 0.207 -999
